<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico completed all five auctions in the secondary market in which it sought to drain 4.397 billion pesos by purchasing paper.</p>
<p>CREDIT AUCTIONS   TERM     MAX    MIN    AVERAGE  BIDS BIDDERS</p>
<p> 1.000  bln pesos  17 days  25.81  25.70  25.75    6    6</p>
<p> 1.000  bln pesos   9 days  25.50  25.44  25.47    8    7</p>
<p> 1.000  bln pesos   6 days  25.30  25.22  25.27    7    7</p>
<p>   698  bln pesos   2 days  25.38  25.30  25.32    4    4</p>
<p>   699  bln pesos   1 day   25.02  24.95  25.01   N/A  N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The maximum, minimum and average are percentages.</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9500))</p>
